## 1. Agreement

By installing, building, accessing or using Kanaru (the "Software"), including
its source code, you agree to this Agreement. If you do not agree, do not use
the Software.

## 2. What you may do

Kanaru is **source available**. Subject to this Agreement, you get a personal,
non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:

- install and use the Software for your own personal, non-commercial use;
- read the source code, build it and modify it for your own personal use;
- modify the source code to contribute changes back to Kanaru (section 8).

## 3. What you may not do

Unless the owner gives you written permission, you may not:

- use the Software, or any part of it, for a commercial purpose;
- redistribute, sublicense, sell, rent or lease the Software, modified or not;
- publish the Software, or a work based on it, under another name, brand,
  owner or license, or as part of another product;
- use the source code, or parts of it, for any purpose other than personal use,
  personal learning or contributing to Kanaru;
- remove or change this Agreement, copyright notices or attributions.

**Exception: official builds.** Unmodified official builds of the Software may
be redistributed free of charge through software stores and repositories that
the owner has approved (for example Google Play or Flathub), as long as the
name, branding and this Agreement stay intact.

## 4. Ownership

The Software and all intellectual property rights in it belong to the owner.
This Agreement grants a license; it does not sell or transfer ownership.

## 5. Third-party components

The Software includes or loads third-party components (for example libmpv and
FFmpeg, Flutter and Dart packages, Rust crates, fonts, and the files under
`rust_builder/cargokit/`). Each of them stays under its own license, which
takes precedence over this Agreement for that component. Their notices are
kept with their source, and the app lists the licenses of the components it
includes (Settings > About > Licenses).

Nothing in this Agreement limits the rights those licenses give you. In
particular, where a component is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public
License (such as the libmpv and FFmpeg builds the app loads), you may replace
or modify that library and reverse engineer the Software as far as needed to
debug such modifications.

## 6. Earlier versions

Versions of this repository published before the effective date were released
under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later. Copies of those
versions that you already received stay under that license. This Agreement
applies to every version from the effective date onward.

## 7. Paid features and accounts

Kanaru may offer optional paid features. They are provided separately, and may
require an account. Paying for them does not change the rights in this
Agreement for the rest of the Software.

## 8. Contributions

Contributions are welcome. By submitting a contribution you agree that it may
be included in the Software under this Agreement. Contributions from people
outside the project need a signed Contributor License Agreement before they
are merged (see `CONTRIBUTING.md`).

## 9. Data and privacy

- The Software collects no analytics, crash reports or usage tracking, and it
  does not send your music or library data anywhere by itself.
- Network access happens only for features you use. Plugins you install send
  data to the hosts they list, which the app shows before you install them.
- If you sign in to an account, the account service stores your email address,
  your devices and your purchases, only to provide the paid features.
- Logs are stored on your device and leave it only if you share them yourself.

## 10. No warranty

The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and
non-infringement.

## 11. Limitation of liability

To the extent allowed by law, the owner is not liable for any damages arising
from the use of, or the inability to use, the Software.

## 12. Termination

This license ends automatically if you break this Agreement. You must then stop
using the Software and delete your copies.

## 13. Changes

The owner may change this Agreement for later versions of the Software. The
version shipped with a release applies to that release.
